 "intro": [
  "\"The members of Jacob's family who went to Egypt were seventy in all\" (46:27): Leah's 33, Zilpah's 16, Rachel's 14 and Bilhah's 7. Seventy matches the seventy nations of Genesis 10: Israel's family stands for all the nations (Deuteronomy 32:8).",
  "Leah's list has only 32 names once Er and Onan, who died in Canaan, are left out. Ibn Ezra counts Jacob himself; Rashi counts Jochebed, Levi's daughter, \"born between the walls\" as they entered Egypt (Numbers 26:59). Acts 7:14, following the Septuagint, gives 75."
 ],
 "countNote": "Filled dots are the seventy. Jacob is counted by some (Ibn Ezra); others count Jochebed in his place (Rashi).",
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Rashi and Ibn Ezra on Genesis 46; Genesis Rabbah 94; Babylonian Talmud, Bava Batra 123b. Parallel lists: Numbers 26; 1 Chronicles 2–8.",
